	(text "Average ESP-01S current requirment is about 100mA.\nFor LDO of ~200mV-300mV and voltage ranges from 4.2V to 3.6V, \nthe power consumtion of the ESP at 100mA is 330mW and the maximum \npower dissipation at the LDO is 0.9V*150mA,or ~135mW, a total of 465mW.\nAdding another 35mW of losses, the total power consumption can be around 500mW.\nA Li-ion battery of 2000mA@4.2V can provide up to 8W, \nso the ESP can last for up to 16hours if the LDO only draws ~150mA/h. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 109.22 20.574 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "13a77e27-135d-447d-98f7-9ba222646a54")
	)
	(text "Buck and Li charger only consume power during daylight"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110.49 66.294 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "1426f3af-7fe9-4a11-bf56-849b20ef77cb")
	)
	(text "P‑MOSFET (AO3413):\nSource (S): to your 4.8-3.6 V supply\nDrain (D): to Vin of the boost converter\nGate (G):\nPull‑up resistor (e.g. 100 kΩ) from Gate to Source\n\nConnected to Drain of 2N7000\nN‑MOSFET (2N7000):\nSource: to GND\nDrain: to Gate of AO3413\nGate: to ESP‑01 GPIO via a small resistor (e.g. 100 Ω)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 113.03 103.632 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 255 54 124 1)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5ca79242-6574-4b35-848c-63c2277f8811")
	)
